    <string name="root_description">Some systems, such as HyperOS, freeze background apps and block their alarms and notification broadcasts. A root watchdog can wake the module at the next scheduled task time even while it is frozen.\nEnabling writes a boot script to /data/adb/service.d; disabling removes it.</string>
    <string name="record_detail_title">%1$s details</string>
    <string name="execution_mode_description">Android mode uses system alarms and background jobs. KSU mode runs the same task logic in an independent module process and can continue after the app is closed.\n\nBoth modes share your local task settings. Switching waits only for the current local execution to finish and save progress, not for a merchant trip or lore reward to become ready. This handoff prevents duplicate execution.\n\nKSU mode is experimental. It requires the companion ZIP, root access for this app, and the primary Android user. Login credentials are copied to root-private files in /data/adb/reamicro-automation (directory 700, files 600). Other apps cannot read them. Switching back to Android syncs the final records and deletes this credential copy.\n\nThe companion module is bundled in the APK. “Use KSU” checks for it and installs it with ksud if needed, then switches modes. If a reboot is requested, reboot the device and select it again.\n\nSleep, lost connectivity, a disabled module, expired tokens, or API restrictions may still delay tasks. A failed check does not automatically switch modes, to avoid duplicate spending. Switch back to Android before uninstalling the KSU module.</string>
